{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SerialExecutor"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Executor","text":"Executor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScF"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Custom-Actor-Executors","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Custom Actor Executors"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, all actor types execute tasks on a shared global concurrent pool."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The global pool does not guarantee any thread (or dispatch queue) affinity,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so actors are free to use different threads as they execute tasks."}]},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The runtime may perform various optimizations to minimize un-necessary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thread switching."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sometimes it is important to be able to customize the execution behavior"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of an actor. For example, when an actor is known to perform heavy blocking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operations (such as IO), and we would like to keep this work "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"off"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the global"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shared pool, as blocking it may prevent other actors from being responsive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can implement a custom executor, by conforming a type to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, and implementing the "},{"code":"enqueue(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once implemented, you can configure an actor to use such executor by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implementing the actor’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Actor\/unownedExecutor","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" computed property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, you could accept an executor in the actor’s initializer,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store it as a variable (in order to retain it for the duration of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"actor’s lifetime), and return it from the "},{"code":"unownedExecutor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property like this:"}]},{"code":["actor MyActor {","  let myExecutor: MyExecutor","","  \/\/ accepts an executor to run this actor on.","  init(executor: MyExecutor) {","    self.myExecutor = executor","  }","","  nonisolated var unownedExecutor: UnownedSerialExecutor {","    self.myExecutor.asUnownedSerialExecutor()","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is also possible to use a form of shared executor, either created as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"global or static property, which you can then re-use for every MyActor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["actor MyActor {","  \/\/ Serial executor reused by *all* instances of MyActor!","  static let sharedMyActorsExecutor = MyExecutor() \/\/ implements SerialExecutor","","","  nonisolated var unownedExecutor: UnownedSerialExecutor {","    Self.sharedMyActorsExecutor.asUnownedSerialExecutor()","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the example above, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all"}]},{"type":"text","text":" “MyActor” instances would be using the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"serial executor, which would result in only one of such actors ever being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run at the same time. This may be useful if some of your code has some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“specific thread” requirement when interoperating with non-Swift runtimes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for example."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnownedSerialExecutor"},{"type":"text","text":" returned by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unownedExecutor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" retain the executor, you must make sure the lifetime of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it extends beyond the lifetime of any actor or task using it, as otherwise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it may attempt to enqueue work on a released executor object, causing a crash."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The executor returned by unownedExecutor "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"must"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" always be the same object,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and returning different executors can lead to unexpected behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, you can also use existing serial executor implementations,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as Dispatch’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSerialQueue"},{"type":"text","text":" or others."}]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Executor","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sendable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SendableMetatype"]},{"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherited By","type":"inheritedBy","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/MainExecutor"]},{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforming Types","type":"conformingTypes","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnimplementedMainExecutor"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"metadata":{"title":"SerialExecutor","externalID":"s:Scf","symbolKind":"protocol","platforms":[{"beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"2.0","unavailable":false}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SerialExecutor"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SerialExecutor"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","modules":[{"name":"Swift","relatedModules":